# Product context

**Biograph** (shown in the UI as "Biograph", Python app name `healthcare`, Build project name fossibleHIS) is an open-source **Hospital Information System (HIS)**. It is a fork of earthians' Marley Health with enhancements from Tacten / fossibleworks. It runs as a **Frappe app on top of ERPNext**, and most of its data model follows **HL7 FHIR**.

## Who uses it
- **Clinic and hospital staff** (practitioners, nurses, lab technicians, front desk, billing) use it in Frappe Desk (`app_home = /desk/healthcare`).
- **Patients** use a Vue patient portal at `/patient-portal`. There they view and book appointments, see diagnostic orders and reports, and pay.

## Main feature areas
Patient management, outpatient appointments (including block-based therapy booking and recurring appointments), inpatient records and occupancy, clinical procedures, rehabilitation and physiotherapy (therapy plans and sessions), laboratory (lab tests, samples, diagnostic reports, observations), medication requests and inpatient medication, insurance (payors, contracts, coverage, claims), fee validity and billing through ERPNext Sales Invoice, medical code standards (Code System / Code Value), patient duplicate checking, and India-specific regional ABDM integration.

ERPNext supplies pharmacy and stock, purchasing, HR, accounts, and assets.

## Fork context
This repo (`fossibleworks/biograph`, main branch `biograph-fh`) is periodically synced with upstream `earthians/marley` `version-16`. When upstream conflicts with the fork, **fork intent wins** (see `wiki/upstream-sync-version-16.md`).
